{
  "_comment": [
      "SDL-670: shared fixture for declarative Element props migrations. The engine test replays it through",
      "migrateElementProps; the Go interpreter (SDL-671, pages-service) is meant to copy it verbatim and replay it too.",
      "Each case: `definition` is an Element as element-catalog.json ships it ({type, propsVersion, migrations});",
      "`node` is a document node; either `expect` (the migrated node, compared as JSON) or `expect_error`",
      "(the error code: migration_count, invalid_step, unknown_custom, newer_version, path_conflict, invalid_version, custom_failed).",
      "The definitions here are TEST Elements (MigrationProbe): no live Element is above propsVersion 1.",
      "Custom ids used here are test-only: every runtime registers its own implementation in its test —",
      "`fixture.join-name`: props.name = props.first + \" \" + props.last, then first and last are removed",
      "(base props only). `fixture.unregistered` is deliberately registered nowhere.",
      "Override layers (member.props, screens[*].props, variants[*].props) are laid over props SHALLOWLY by top-level key;",
      "hence a nested setDefault also goes into every layer holding the path's top-level key, and a nested move seeds a layer",
      "missing the target's top-level key with a copy of the base's (already migrated) value; a layer WITHOUT the move's source",
      "(and not holding the source's top-level key) that holds the target's top-level object gets the base's PRE-step value in the",
      "target. In an override layer a non-object on the path is skipped for setDefault and for that carried base value; a move",
      "whose source IS in the layer and whose target parent there is a non-object is path_conflict (skipping would lose the value).",
      "Paths go through objects only.",
      "Known limits pinned by cases: a move out of a nested object lets the base value show through a layer that hid it; a screen",
      "layer gets the base's value, not the member branch's; a seeded layer keeps a copy of the base's siblings.",
      "A node already at the definition's version comes back unchanged without the definition being checked.",
      "A step carrying a field its op does not take, or a migration carrying anything but `steps`, is invalid_step."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {"name": "rename a top-level key, in every props layer", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "rename", "from": "title", "to": "heading"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"title": "Hello", "tone": "info"}, "member": {"props": {"title": "Hello, member"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"title": "Hi"}}}, "variants": [{"when": {"field": "x", "op": "exists"}, "props": {"title": "V"}}]}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"heading": "Hello", "tone": "info"}, "member": {"props": {"heading": "Hello, member"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"heading": "Hi"}}}, "variants": [{"when": {"field": "x", "op": "exists"}, "props": {"heading": "V"}}]}},
    {"name": "rename a nested key keeps it in the same object; an absent source is a no-op", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "rename", "from": "source.coll", "to": "collection"}, {"op": "rename", "from": "missing", "to": "still_missing"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"source": {"coll": "posts", "limit": 5}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"source": {"collection": "posts", "limit": 5}}}},
    {"name": "remove a key, top-level and nested; an absent key is a no-op", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "remove", "key": "legacy"}, {"op": "remove", "key": "source.project_id"}, {"op": "remove", "key": "nope.deeper"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"legacy": true, "keep": 1, "source": {"project_id": "p", "collection": "c"}}, "screens": {"desktop": {"props": {"legacy": false}}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"keep": 1, "source": {"collection": "c"}}, "screens": {"desktop": {"props": {}}}}},
    {"name": "a top-level setDefault writes the base only (a layer without the key falls back to it), creating objects on the way; present values (null included) stay", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "setDefault", "key": "size", "value": "md"}, {"op": "setDefault", "key": "tone", "value": "info"}, {"op": "setDefault", "key": "empty", "value": "x"}, {"op": "setDefault", "key": "layout.columns", "value": [1, 2]}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"tone": "danger", "empty": null}, "member": {"props": {"tone": "success"}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"tone": "danger", "empty": null, "size": "md", "layout": {"columns": [1, 2]}}, "member": {"props": {"tone": "success"}}}},
    {"name": "setDefault on a node without props creates them", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "setDefault", "key": "size", "value": "md"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe"}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"size": "md"}}},
    {"name": "mapValue replaces known string values in every layer; unknown and non-string values stay", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "mapValue", "key": "variant", "map": {"primary": "default", "danger": "destructive", "off": null}}, {"op": "mapValue", "key": "count", "map": {"1": "one"}}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"variant": "primary", "count": 1}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"variant": "danger"}}, "tablet": {"props": {"variant": "ghost"}}, "desktop": {"props": {"variant": "off"}}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"variant": "default", "count": 1}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"variant": "destructive"}}, "tablet": {"props": {"variant": "ghost"}}, "desktop": {"props": {"variant": null}}}}},
    {"name": "move to a nested path creates the objects on the way and replaces a present target", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "collection", "to": "source.collection"}, {"op": "move", "from": "limit", "to": "source.limit"}, {"op": "move", "from": "gone", "to": "source.gone"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"collection": "posts", "limit": 10, "source": {"limit": 3}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"source": {"collection": "posts", "limit": 10}}}},
    {"name": "move out of a nested object to the top level", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "style.align", "to": "align"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"style": {"align": "center", "gap": 4}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"style": {"gap": 4}, "align": "center"}}},
    {"name": "move into a path held by a non-object is a path_conflict", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "collection", "to": "source.collection"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"collection": "posts", "source": "legacy-string"}}, "expect_error": "path_conflict"},
    {"name": "custom step runs the registered implementation", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "custom", "id": "fixture.join-name"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"first": "Ada", "last": "Lovelace", "age": 36}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"name": "Ada Lovelace", "age": 36}}},
    {"name": "custom step with an unregistered id is an explicit error", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "custom", "id": "fixture.unregistered"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect_error": "unknown_custom"},
    {"name": "chain v1 -> v4: each migration applied in order, steps in order", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 4, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "rename", "from": "title", "to": "heading"}, {"op": "setDefault", "key": "size", "value": "md"}]}, {"steps": [{"op": "mapValue", "key": "size", "map": {"md": "medium"}}, {"op": "move", "from": "heading", "to": "text.heading"}]}, {"steps": [{"op": "custom", "id": "fixture.join-name"}, {"op": "remove", "key": "legacy"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"title": "T", "first": "Grace", "last": "Hopper", "legacy": 1}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 4, "props": {"text": {"heading": "T"}, "size": "medium", "name": "Grace Hopper"}}},
    {"name": "chain starts at the node's own version (v2 -> v4 skips the first migration)", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 4, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "rename", "from": "title", "to": "heading"}, {"op": "setDefault", "key": "size", "value": "md"}]}, {"steps": [{"op": "mapValue", "key": "size", "map": {"md": "medium"}}, {"op": "move", "from": "heading", "to": "text.heading"}]}, {"steps": [{"op": "remove", "key": "legacy"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"title": "kept: v2 has no title rule", "heading": "H", "size": "md", "legacy": 1}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 4, "props": {"title": "kept: v2 has no title rule", "text": {"heading": "H"}, "size": "medium"}}},
    {"name": "a node at the definition's version comes back unchanged", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "remove", "key": "a"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"a": 1}}},
    {"name": "a node newer than the definition is refused", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": []}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 3, "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect_error": "newer_version"},
    {"name": "propsVersion 2 without a migration is refused", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": []}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect_error": "migration_count"},
    {"name": "an unknown op is refused", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "explode", "key": "a"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect_error": "invalid_step"},
    {"name": "rename.to must be a key name, not a path", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "rename", "from": "a", "to": "b.c"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect_error": "invalid_step"},
    {"name": "setDefault with a nested key also fills override layers that hold the parent object (shallow overlay)", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "setDefault", "key": "source.limit", "value": 10}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"source": {"coll": "a"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "b"}}}, "tablet": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "c", "limit": 3}}}}, "member": {"props": {"other": 1}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"source": {"coll": "a", "limit": 10}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "b", "limit": 10}}}, "tablet": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "c", "limit": 3}}}}, "member": {"props": {"other": 1}}}},
    {"name": "move into a nested path seeds an override layer's missing parent from the base, siblings kept", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "limit", "to": "source.limit"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"limit": 3, "source": {"coll": "a"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"limit": 5}}, "tablet": {"props": {"limit": 7, "source": {"coll": "t"}}}, "desktop": {"props": {"gap": 1}}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"source": {"coll": "a", "limit": 3}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "a", "limit": 5}}}, "tablet": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "t", "limit": 7}}}, "desktop": {"props": {"gap": 1}}}}},
    {"name": "rename onto an existing key overwrites it", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "rename", "from": "a", "to": "b"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1, "b": 2}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"b": 1}}},
    {"name": "move a -> a.b wraps the value", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "a", "to": "a.b"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 5, "c": 1}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"a": {"b": 5}, "c": 1}}},
    {"name": "reading through an array finds nothing: remove, mapValue, rename are no-ops", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "remove", "key": "items.0"}, {"op": "remove", "key": "items.x"}, {"op": "mapValue", "key": "items.0", "map": {"a": "b"}}, {"op": "rename", "from": "items.0", "to": "first"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"items": ["a", "b"]}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"items": ["a", "b"]}}},
    {"name": "writing through an array is a path_conflict", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "setDefault", "key": "items.x", "value": 1}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"items": []}}, "expect_error": "path_conflict"},
    {"name": "a v1 node of a v1 definition comes back unchanged", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 1, "migrations": []}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1}}},
    {"name": "node propsVersion 0 is invalid_version", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": []}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 0, "props": {}}, "expect_error": "invalid_version"},
    {"name": "node propsVersion -1 is invalid_version", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": []}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": -1, "props": {}}, "expect_error": "invalid_version"},
    {"name": "node propsVersion 1.5 is invalid_version", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": []}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 1.5, "props": {}}, "expect_error": "invalid_version"},
    {"name": "a step with a field its op does not take is invalid_step", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "remove", "key": "a", "note": "leaks into the catalog"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect_error": "invalid_step"},
    {"name": "a migration with anything but steps is invalid_step", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [], "why": "x"}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect_error": "invalid_step"},
    {"name": "nested setDefault skips an override layer that holds a non-object on the path", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "setDefault", "key": "source.limit", "value": 10}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"source": {"coll": "a"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": null}}, "tablet": {"props": {"source": "legacy"}}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"source": {"coll": "a", "limit": 10}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": null}}, "tablet": {"props": {"source": "legacy"}}}}},
    {"name": "nested move: a layer holding the target's parent but not the source gets the base's pre-step value (probe C)", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "limit", "to": "source.limit"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"limit": 3, "source": {"coll": "a"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "b"}}}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"source": {"coll": "a", "limit": 3}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "b", "limit": 3}}}}}},
    {"name": "nested move across member and screen layers: the screen gets the base's value, not the member's (probe F, known limit)", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "limit", "to": "source.limit"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"limit": 3, "source": {"coll": "a"}}, "member": {"props": {"limit": 4}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "m"}}}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"source": {"coll": "a", "limit": 3}}, "member": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "a", "limit": 4}}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"source": {"coll": "m", "limit": 3}}}}}},
    {"name": "nested move: a layer that hid the source (holds its parent) does not get the base's value", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "style.align", "to": "source.align"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"style": {"align": "c"}, "source": {"coll": "a"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"style": {"gap": 8}, "source": {"coll": "b"}}}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"style": {}, "source": {"coll": "a", "align": "c"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"style": {"gap": 8}, "source": {"coll": "b"}}}}}},
    {"name": "move out of a nested object to the top level: the base value now shows through a layer that hid it (probe D, known limit)", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "style.align", "to": "align"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"style": {"align": "center", "gap": 4}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"style": {"gap": 8}}}}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"style": {"gap": 4}, "align": "center"}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"style": {"gap": 8}}}}}},
    {"name": "a node at the definition's version comes back unchanged even when the definition is malformed", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": []}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"a": 1}}, "expect": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "props": {"a": 1}}},
    {"name": "move with the source in an override layer whose target parent is a string is a path_conflict", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "limit", "to": "source.limit"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"limit": 3, "source": {"coll": "a"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"limit": 5, "source": "legacy"}}}}, "expect_error": "path_conflict"},
    {"name": "move with the source in an override layer whose target parent is null is a path_conflict", "definition": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "propsVersion": 2, "migrations": [{"steps": [{"op": "move", "from": "limit", "to": "source.limit"}]}]}, "node": {"type": "MigrationProbe", "props": {"limit": 3, "source": {"coll": "a"}}, "screens": {"mobile": {"props": {"limit": 5, "source": null}}}}, "expect_error": "path_conflict"}
  ]
